  "body": "The last part of #692 still owed: arc and circle centres from a round feature edge, offered as **feature points** only where a picker asks for them. Branched from upstream `main` at 8174f37d (the newest tag reachable from it is v0.18.0).\n\n## What changed\n- **Pick service (`crates/app/src/pick/`)**\n  - New `centre.rs` with `centre_selection`, `centre_of` and `centre_point`. A centre pick is stored as the round run it comes from (`FeatureSel::Chain(run)`) and read back through #759's `circle_of_run`. A straight or non-circular run is refused by name, wrapping `CircleRefusal`.\n  - `selection_of` now maps a `Centre` target to that run. Before, it returned `None`.\n  - `circle_centre_in` is `circle_centre` with the frame passed in, so point slots can read the centre in the document frame.\n  - **Visibility:** a centre is offered when its *edge* is in sight. Up to 8 segment midpoints around the run are tested; the centre's own position is not. Pick-through works as before.\n  - **Snap sort:** ray distance is compared to the nanometre, so two centres stacked on one axis tie and the nearer one wins. Before, float noise could pick the far rim.\n- **Opt-in, not a global change:** `PickKinds::ALL` still leaves centres out. In `feature_click::ask` only two pickers ask for them: the three-points draft (in Vertex mode) and an axis by two points. The plain pick modes, the plane row, an axis by edge, fixture locate and the WCS role draft never snap to a centre.\n- **Point slots:** `pick::points` (three points) and `pick::axis` (a pair of points) read a circular edge chain as its centre and refuse any other edge by name. `points_pick::take` and `axis_pick::take` accept a centre and refuse a straight edge with the reason. The axis readout shows a centre as a point.\n- **MCP:** `lay_part_on_points` and `set_part_axes` (point pairs) accept a circular-edge chain id for its centre, through the same functions. Tool descriptions and the camcraft-mcp skill rows are updated. `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` goes from 54 to 55 (a process file changed; settled at merge).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/692-centre-points.md`. It records why there is no new `FeatureSel` variant and no `centre:` id form.\n\n## Pins (each one was mutation-checked: guard removed, test red, guard restored)\n| Pin | Test | Mutation |\n|---|---|---|\n| A round edge gives its centre when the picker opts in | `centre_pick::a_round_edge_yields_its_centre_when_the_picker_opts_in` | `selection_of` Centre -> `None`: red |\n| A picker that doesn't opt in never gets a centre | `centre_pick::a_picker_that_does_not_opt_in_never_gets_a_centre`, ui `vertex_pick_tests::only_the_point_takers_that_read_a_centre_ask_for_centres` | centre tier also offered for points/edges: red; `ask` opt-in line removed: ui red |\n| A straight edge is refused by name | `centre_pick::a_straight_edge_is_refused_by_name` | straight check in `circle_of_run` removed: red |\n| A hidden round edge's centre: not offered with Pick-through off, offered with it on (ortho and perspective) | `centre_pick::a_hidden_round_edge_offers_its_centre_only_when_picking_through` | edge-visibility check replaced by `true`: red |\n| The MCP centre pick goes through the same service and refuses by name | `centre_pick::mcp_point_picks_take_a_round_edge_centre_and_refuse_a_straight_one_by_name`, `centre_pick::three_points_read_a_round_edge_as_its_centre` | `centre_point` guard in `pick::points` removed: red |\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. It ran 20 app suites (pick, align, MCP align/setup/WCS, fixture locate and others) and the ui lib.\n- The full ui lib run single-threaded from `crates/ui`: 663 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The GUI by hand: hovering at a hole's middle in the three-points and two-points rows, and the rim highlight on hover. The maintainer's GUI hand check for #692 is still owed, which is why this PR says `Refs`.\n- The fixture-locate mates and the WCS role draft do not opt in yet (see the decision file).\n\nChangelog: Picking - in the three-points and axis-by-two-points picks (GUI and MCP), a hole rim or boss edge now gives its circle centre as a point; a straight edge is refused by name (#692, PR #1405)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #692\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
